{
    "word": "solitariness",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "18045241-5fa4-3394-8476-97b234bfc7ba",
                "word": "solitariness",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "58ebc10d-6853-4f6f-9866-4d76d5d5625a",
                        "entry_id": "18045241-5fa4-3394-8476-97b234bfc7ba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "solitarinesses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e745e8bb-05a2-388d-bf46-0254f60fc370",
                        "entry_id": "18045241-5fa4-3394-8476-97b234bfc7ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or quality of being solitary."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1125f793-258c-442e-9888-2cbd2b5c93e3",
                                "sense_id": "e745e8bb-05a2-388d-bf46-0254f60fc370",
                                "text": "In both a mazefull ſolitarineſſe: / In night of ſprites the gaſtly powers to ſtur, / In thee or ſprites or ſprited gaſtlineſſe: […]",
                                "translation": "The New Arcadia",
                                "english": "The New Arcadia"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3f6d4e5-895d-42b5-b0c8-059e4da5387d",
                                "sense_id": "e745e8bb-05a2-388d-bf46-0254f60fc370",
                                "text": "I saw a Deane of S. Hillarie of Poictiers, reduced by reason and the incommoditie of his melancholy to such a continuall solitarinesse, that when I entered into his chamber he had never removed one step out of it in two and twenty yeares before[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce927513-53e1-456f-8d48-4dc33886b62c",
                                "sense_id": "e745e8bb-05a2-388d-bf46-0254f60fc370",
                                "text": "So much as doing good is better than not doing evil, will I account Christian good fellowship better than an eremitish and melancholy solitariness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "63c7eb7d-74d3-4ef0-8d1c-80de8cf7cb4a",
                        "source_entry_id": "18045241-5fa4-3394-8476-97b234bfc7ba",
                        "source_sense_id": "e745e8bb-05a2-388d-bf46-0254f60fc370",
                        "source_sense_description": "state or quality of being solitary",
                        "target_lang_word": "solitarisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "solitarisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a5f1c37-08fa-3e35-9d0d-830132116808",
                                        "entry_id": "e4404659-22ab-3c4a-a590-e159630d4bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Disposition d’esprit qui pousse à vivre à l’écart des autres."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c459b93-6d96-430e-ac84-de220f36aef8",
                                                "sense_id": "4a5f1c37-08fa-3e35-9d0d-830132116808",
                                                "text": "Chez certaines espèces, les tendances au solitarisme sont assez fortes pour ne pas permettre un rapprochement même temporaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b35489b1-6192-4c16-b3ff-22b774be36a6",
                                                "sense_id": "4a5f1c37-08fa-3e35-9d0d-830132116808",
                                                "text": "Ce peut être soit un solitarisme de fait (le sujet vivant seul), soit un solitarisme relatif, avec, dans le groupe où l’individu se trouve plus ou moins agrégé, un détachement à l’égard des autres."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26e94dd0-f36f-3271-be17-2f054ccf21de",
                                        "entry_id": "e4404659-22ab-3c4a-a590-e159630d4bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Comportement solitaire pathologique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "568c5ac9-3ca1-4b70-bd24-142f8edb905c",
                                                "sense_id": "26e94dd0-f36f-3271-be17-2f054ccf21de",
                                                "text": "II a été ainsi amené à une conduite de repliement, de solitarisme des jeux et, plus gâté par ses sœurs, d’affinités pour les occupations tranquilles, domestiques et ménagères, avec ceux qui ne le moquent pas et où il n’a pas à parler."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4d696b9-dfc4-46ea-bc7f-db690eb56554",
                        "source_entry_id": "18045241-5fa4-3394-8476-97b234bfc7ba",
                        "source_sense_id": "e745e8bb-05a2-388d-bf46-0254f60fc370",
                        "source_sense_description": "state or quality of being solitary",
                        "target_lang_word": "Einsamkeit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Einsamkeit",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                        "entry_id": "44c4a7d3-0cc8-372a-924b-404455c280f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "das Alleinsein oder Verlassensein"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80b5b1cf-8279-4d9d-9d9b-3ba7507e86fd",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "\"Einsamkeit hat viele Namen,",
                                                "translation": "das verlorene Glück, die endlose Zeit ohne Dich. ..\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6b8d384-9f7f-4787-97be-578cfedd726a",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "„Die grassierende Einsamkeit muss furchtbar sein.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d882ccdc-ac12-470d-a67a-6bc355304fc6",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "„Dort sind es die Raben, die auf Befehl Gottes dem Propheten in der Einsamkeit an einem Bach Brot und Fleisch bringen, ihn ernähren.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39bc9ba6-1cf8-4d59-a9a7-ed52a6a53882",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "„Die Einsamkeit raubte ihre Kräfte und folterte sie, dennoch meinte sie sie nicht entbehren zu können.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93b74faf-d8b1-448d-bf1c-dfac771cf804",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "„Einsamkeit ist ein gesamtgesellschaftliches Phänomen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "051b8598-297d-4397-8fdf-62031fd94563",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "„Neu ist, dass nicht mehr nur Alte oder Kranke von Einsamkeit betroffen sind, sondern auch die Jungen – und das in großer Zahl.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88910aa8-7fcf-4d4f-a4e4-fc3668ded0d3",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "„Wenn die Einsamkeit nicht nur anklopft, wenn man allein in einem Hotelzimmer liegt, sondern ins Leben einzieht, kann sie krank machen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "318ec17b-0c70-45bc-8f31-92b844bc9c56",
                                                "sense_id": "1653c894-5e63-3961-8041-4d4d9972ecfe",
                                                "text": "„In Großbritannien gibt es weltweit die erste Ministerin gegen Einsamkeit.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b7bc76a-e11f-3f2b-912c-642c04f50568",
